# Do not start runs

Unless the user **explicitly** asks to launch/start/kick off a run:

- **Do not** start training, eval, finetune, paper_eval suites, wandb syncing jobs, or other long GPU/CPU runs.
- **Do** wire configs, materialize YAMLs, register suites, compare HPs/architecture, and print the exact command for the user to run.
- “Wire up”, “set up”, “prepare”, “add a config/suite” ≠ permission to launch.
- If a run was started by mistake: stop it immediately and report where it was pointed (local log path + wandb entity/project/run URL if any).
